3","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-122433","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":278,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-103017","title":"Hide and Seek","authors":["All Children Reading Cambodia"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Dodo plays Hide-and-seek with mum, what can Dodo find?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/150992/size7/efc8b1d281e3853492ad0e1ee0651268.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/150992/size7/efc8b1d281e3853492ad0e1ee0651268.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-103017","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-103017","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":279,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-14051","title":"The Best Thing Ever","authors":["Melissa  Fagan","Stefania Origgi"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Muzi loves to build with his toys. But when he leaves them behind to travel to uGogo’s house, he discovers something very special about the world. And he learns something new about himself.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/118153/size7/bc2ba70b6ef08fef7c20b01264e48156.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/118153/size7/bc2ba70b6ef08fef7c20b01264e48156.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-14051","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-14051","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":280,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-93901","title":"Making Friends with Snakes (But from a Distance)","authors":["Rohan Chakravarty"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Naagin and Dhaman are here to make friends with you, but from a distance. After all, they are snakes. Find out everything you wanted to know about these beautiful reptiles and also learn how to stay safe and let snakes slither to safety!","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727062/size7/1434dec5e0d6a834070c3f6555c82bc2.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727062/size7/1434dec5e0d6a834070c3f6555c82bc2.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-93901","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-93901","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":281,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-31137","title":"Who Made the Tomato Chutney?","authors":["Kavitha Mandana"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Tara and Ravi go to the market to buy fruits and vegetables. But each time one fruit gets squashed! The concept of sorting is introduced through heavy and light objects. \nThe illustrations in the book were made using bits of paper, old magazines and paper bags that were collected - not squished - under mattresses.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/717010/size7/0bef1395055c740659b27b823aeea0ac.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/717010/size7/0bef1395055c740659b27b823aeea0ac.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-31137","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-31137","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":282,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-10058","title":"Biju Spins Some Magic","authors":["Jaya Jaitly"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Biju and his family are weavers in rural Odisha. They create beautiful fabrics to sell in the cities of India and abroad. This is the tale of Biju’s adventures when he accompanies his father to Delhi to sell the saris, and in the process impresses a city boy with his skill. Jaya Jaitly’s fun-filled story is illustrated by Bhramara Nayak in the patachitra style.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/524535/size7/2d6162e002a3bf3ad6834ac1a6050a54.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/524535/size7/2d6162e002a3bf3ad6834ac1a6050a54.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-10058","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-10058","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":283,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-212","title":"The Tree","authors":["Madhav Chavan"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"The tale of how a tree grows from a tiny seed.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/722234/size7/94ca99b3484af2b07528283397858dba.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/722234/size7/94ca99b3484af2b07528283397858dba.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-212","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-212","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":284,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-110883","title":"Water Dance","authors":["Sean D'mello"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Guddu can dance to anything. Today he has found music in water and can’t stop doing a jig as he makes his way down a stream. A story that introduces water bodies and celebrates the joy of water.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/721324/size7/5a1f19ca4a60e1aaf734bc03f0c3be11.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/721324/size7/5a1f19ca4a60e1aaf734bc03f0c3be11.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-110883","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-110883","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":285,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-754","title":"Marching to Freedom","authors":["Subhadra Sen Gupta"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Mahatma Gandhi and his followers have decided to march to Dandi to protest against the unfair salt tax imposed by the British. 9-year-old Dhani who lives at the Sabarmati Ashram wants to go too. This tale captures the spirit behind the momentous event that inspired millions of Indians to join the struggle for Independence.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/703496/size7/e199c7b11d12f05af68f797c629d0af3.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/703496/size7/e199c7b11d12f05af68f797c629d0af3.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-754","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-754","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":286,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-339149","title":"Have You Ever Climbed a Tree?","authors":["Priyadarshini Gogoi"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Have you ever climbed a tree? Riniki dreams of climbing trees all over the country. Join her as she scrambles, crawls and clambers on the jackfruit, the chinar, the khejri and other trees.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/495551/size7/2d67536698e82439794800d91ba40bef.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/495551/size7/2d67536698e82439794800d91ba40bef.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-339149","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-339149","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":287,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-342334","title":"Plants Are Everywhere","authors":["Ritu Desai"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Plants grow everywhere — on high mountains, on arid lands, and even under the sea. Explore different types of plants in this book.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/434073/size7/3927b068f2f1009ae79ef445c56eb5be.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/434073/size7/3927b068f2f1009ae79ef445c56eb5be.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-342334","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-342334","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":288,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-4314","title":"How Do Aeroplanes Fly?","authors":["Aditi Sarawagi"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Sarla wished she could fly high like an eagle or like an aeroplane. Of course you can fly, said her new teacher. Here, Sarla shares all that she has learnt about flight and aeroplanes.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/711239/size7/76fe943740d2496ae267805d81599763.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/711239/size7/76fe943740d2496ae267805d81599763.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-4314","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-4314","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":289,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-664","title":"Three for Free - A Folktale from Taiwan","authors":["Greystroke"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Once upon a time, in a little village by a mountain, an old man came to sell his dumplings. He sold one for one cent, two for two cents and three for free! As the villagers started gobbling up the dumplings three at a time, strange things started happening around them. Read this tantalising tale from Taiwan to see what happened in this village by the Ban Pin Shan Mountain!","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/699933/size7/53190cd41d58e95d07ea58dae0b26e02.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/699933/size7/53190cd41d58e95d07ea58dae0b26e02.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-664","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-664","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":290,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-13262","title":"The Best House of All","authors":["Natasha Sharma"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Big, small, round, square, heavy, light... homes can be of many kinds! Find out why each home is different, and build your own home. Our little architect shows you how!","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/724108/size7/44fe170ad046b14664899d1727befc14.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/724108/size7/44fe170ad046b14664899d1727befc14.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-13262","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-13262","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":291,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-3841","title":"Why Does A Poori Puff Up?","authors":["Varsha  Joshi"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Round, fat pooris are a treat in most Indian homes. Why do they puff? There is a whole lot of science behind this simple question.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/712715/size7/ff6bc354d6dd3c347b5b06c130c85cd2.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/712715/size7/ff6bc354d6dd3c347b5b06c130c85cd2.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-3841","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-3841","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":292,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-1067","title":"Naughty Dog","authors":["Kanchan Bannerjee"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"If you had a tail, you would wag it after reading this book. This book is one of the four books in the 'Animals Around Us' series.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/704905/size7/6ba1aebea83f179aa77599f8f256fc8d.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/704905/size7/6ba1aebea83f179aa77599f8f256fc8d.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-1067","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-1067","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":293,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-8828","title":"Maaloo, Kaaloo ...and who?","authors":["Manisha Chaudhry"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Maaloo and Kaaloo are back! This time they are playing detective at Grandma’s house in the hills.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/722825/size7/a8f6d625f16864f8d814762e38c0e384.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/722825/size7/a8f6d625f16864f8d814762e38c0e384.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-8828","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-8828","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":294,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-266069","title":"Our Beautiful World","authors":["Bibek Bhattacharya"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Humans have been around for 2,00,000 years. But in the last 250 years, we have created a monster: climate change. This monster is making the planet hotter, and threatening the lives of those we share the planet with. How did we get here? And what comes next? This non-fiction book tells us why we should be hot under the collar about the climate crisis.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/621795/size7/bf212bf61e522b6f4d6d83b07ad4934f.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/621795/size7/bf212bf61e522b6f4d6d83b07ad4934f.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-266069","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-266069","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":295,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-24769","title":"Keya's Day at the Beach","authors":["Radha Rangarajan"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Join Keya the Soldier Crab as she explores the beach with her Ma, and meets many different crabs.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/714194/size7/56f741bbf87a304122d2aa03d106d334.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/714194/size7/56f741bbf87a304122d2aa03d106d334.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-24769","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/