ring kulfi! How many kulfis should Bhanwari buy?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/715260/size7/21022b43ed0c07247343a2f2b5de77f9.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/715260/size7/21022b43ed0c07247343a2f2b5de77f9.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-111783","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-111783","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":328,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-91871","title":"Sringeri Srinivas's Cow Must Moo!","authors":["Rohini Nilekani"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Sringeri Srinivas is back with a new problem. His cow has stopped mooing and he is very angry. The farmer frowns at her. His children feed her sweets. But the cow does not moo. Join this lovable farmer's family and his new cat Manuli, in this tale with a twist.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/703876/size7/b8450198b14417eb987648711d009944.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/703876/size7/b8450198b14417eb987648711d009944.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-91871","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-91871","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":329,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-111755","title":"Rainbow Girls","authors":["Kamla Bhasin"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Are all girls alike? Do they like the same things, should they all dress similarly? Let's think about it.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/723769/size7/9f2d836cd9446a608320018eb9b12086.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/723769/size7/9f2d836cd9446a608320018eb9b12086.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-111755","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-111755","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":330,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-119223","title":"The Time-Travelling River","authors":["Parinita Shetty"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Imagine all the stories rivers could tell us about the past, present and future!\nRivers were there when humans wanted to grow food. They were there when humans started to build cities. They are still here, providing water, food and livelihoods. But they are also being treated like rubbish bins. Rivers know how to take care of us, but if we want a future with them, maybe it is time for humans to take care of our precious water bodies.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/196531/size7/011dc21c4087678d4acf7f20de6a0ff6.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/196531/size7/011dc21c4087678d4acf7f20de6a0ff6.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-119223","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-119223","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":331,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-113431","title":"Home","authors":["Fausto Aarya De Santis"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Hasina and her family live happily in their rainy village. Until one day the tides turn, and Amma and young Hasina are swept away by fear. They join a river of escaping people. They become refugees in a new country, away from everything that is familiar. A story that explores the meaning of home.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/518337/size7/f324e69b9a98fdcaed6a391bcd6c4412.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/518337/size7/f324e69b9a98fdcaed6a391bcd6c4412.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-113431","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-113431","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":332,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-13814","title":"A Tiny Seed: The Story of Wangari Maathai","authors":["Nicola  Rijsdijk"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"In a village on the slopes of Mount Kenya, a little girl worked in the fields with her mother. She worried as she saw the big forests disappearing, but she knew the power of a tiny seed.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/38302/size7/5d549c1f79ee67ff88457eb15e032565.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/38302/size7/5d549c1f79ee67ff88457eb15e032565.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-13814","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-13814","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":333,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-103141","title":"Let's Count Legs","authors":["All Children Reading Cambodia"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Whose legs are these? Let's count them!","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/527520/size7/597c7c2e4a75d9b72656ffce8afbca3a.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/527520/size7/597c7c2e4a75d9b72656ffce8afbca3a.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-103141","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-103141","type":"application/epub+zi