.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/55823/size7/7a98e95badfcfc3d0de61368a90d57a2.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-26976","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-26976","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":436,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-37276","title":"A Day at the Carnival","authors":["Alisha Berger"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"The three mice brothers can’t wait to visit the carnival. They ride toy cars, go on the Ferris wheel, and visit the balloon shop. After some time, they realize their youngest brother is missing! Where can he be?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/93876/size7/a434ae08226f7e4fb4da5b52fb4e12b5.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/93876/size7/a434ae08226f7e4fb4da5b52fb4e12b5.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-37276","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-37276","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":437,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-351653","title":"Gola Gola","authors":["Aithihya Ashok Kumar"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Everyone wants a different-coloured gola from the mela! If only there were an easier way for Mariyu to remember all of their choices? A story that introduces the concept of Venn diagrams.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727386/size7/4ef251bd361e98a2383d82fc2c944bdd.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727386/size7/4ef251bd361e98a2383d82fc2c944bdd.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-351653","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-351653","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":438,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-94","title":"The Cat in the Ghat!","authors":["Ambika Rao"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"This is a book that takes you deep into the jungles of the Western Ghats. A wildlife photographer sets out to find an elusive wild cat and meets a menagerie of fascinating creatures. Quirky illustrations pepper a funny narrative inspired by real-life adventure. What better way to invite you to join his quest!","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/705394/size7/727a9682449af6477cf264ce568270af.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/705394/size7/727a9682449af6477cf264ce568270af.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-94","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-94","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":439,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-213112","title":"The Balloon Man","authors":["Kratika Pande"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Chiku buys a balloon and also asks her friends to buy some. But her friends could not buy the balloons because…read more to find out!","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/283788/size7/b5f465a5feaef361a1e4f8086ade0bd8.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/283788/size7/b5f465a5feaef361a1e4f8086ade0bd8.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-213112","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-213112","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":440,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-361239","title":"North, South, East, West","authors":["C G Salamander"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Shaana is travelling the length and breadth of the country with her parents, exploring the many landscapes and peoplescapes of India. She documents her travels in letters that she writes to her friends back at school. A book that explores directions.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/508948/size7/47c601170f2cd0624cf961fb4cfb77a1.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/508948/size7/47c601170f2cd0624cf961fb4cfb77a1.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-361239","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-361239","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":441,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-43617","title":"Our Friends in the Wild","authors":["Shannon David"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Throughout time, people have shared a strong relationship with animals in nature. This non-fiction poem explores the many ways that animals help humans.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/99533/size7/0da7a566a04002a3cab59345951503b8.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/99533/size7/0da7a566a04002a3cab59345951503b8.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-43617","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-43617","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":442,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-43001","title":"Think Before You Act","authors":["Rose Larsen"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"A man takes advice from his friend without thinking twice about it himself. Where do you think this will lead him?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/99516/size7/5717eeb81f7e16ed04c71d00881764bb.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/99516/size7/5717eeb81f7e16ed04c71d00881764bb.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-43001","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-43001","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":443,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-28267","title":"No!","authors":["Liora  Friedland"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"A certain little girl is in the habit of saying ‘No’.\nShe says it a lot. In fact, all of the time.\nOne day though, she is faced with a very tempting\nquestion and can’t help but say ‘YES!’\nPerhaps saying ‘Yes’ isn’t so bad after all.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/85547/size7/cb5c48958330ae0451c7e991cac72821.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/85547/size7/cb5c48958330ae0451c7e991cac72821.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-28267","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-28267","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":444,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-111756","title":"Rainbow Boys","authors":["Kamla Bhasin"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Are all boys alike? Do they like the same things, should they dress similarly? Let's think about it.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/723770/size7/fab09d57400d0f6d7f10b7f68743025d.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/723770/size7/fab09d57400d0f6d7f10b7f68743025d.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-111756","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-111756","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":445,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-921","title":"Samira's Awful Lunch","authors":["Bharati Jagannathan"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Samira doesn't like the lunch her mother has packed in her tiffin box. All her animal friends feel bad for her and offer her their lunch. Read all about Samira's lunchtime adventure...","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/705275/size7/7aa1e49b58c73404d3c1206fe2389c8e.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/705275/size7/7aa1e49b58c73404d3c1206fe2389c8e.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-921","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-921","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":446,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-959","title":"I Am Not Afraid!","authors":["Mini Shrinivasan"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"A little girl goes out alone in the dark. What does she find? This book is one of the four books in the 'Growing Up' series.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/705396/size7/184db2e732a8ca7d0d9383e42d4f043d.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/705396/size7/184db2e732a8ca7d0d9383e42d4f043d.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-959","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-959","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":447,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-13933","title":"Londi: The Dreaming Girl","authors":["Nathalie  Koenig"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Londi loves to dream all day. But where will her dreams take her?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/38927/size7/d9f1f12d9a19adc9cc5babaaa6e0a299.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/38927/size7/d9f1f12d9a19adc9cc5babaaa6e0a299.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-13933","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-13933","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":448,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-104751","title":"Piku's Little World","authors":["Somak Ghoshal"],"language":"","readingLevel":"reading","publisher":"","summary":"Piku loves long summer afternoons, and\ndislikes dark summer evenings. But his\nafternoons become darker when, all of\na sudden, there is no one to read Piku a\nstory. Will Piku’s books remain unread?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/157681/size7/ba42069ffa44213dbf0574fc90eefab9.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/157681/size7/ba42069ffa44213dbf0574fc90eefab9.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-104751","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-104751","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":449,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-132","title":"Daddy's Mo","authors":["Sai Keskar"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"What does Anu like the most about her dad? His Mo! Do you know what a Mo is? Actually, Anu likes everyone with a Mo. So much so that when she sees a Mo, she gets funny ideas!","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/721686/size7/0eaa2e9b2d4d4c465ba2c5e05a6f092c.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/721686/size7/0eaa2e9b2d4d4c465ba2c5e05a6f092c.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-132","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-132","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":450,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-58551","title":"Hungry on the Steps","authors":["Nandini Nayar"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Pranav is hungry. As he climbs up the steps to his house slowly, many others join the line behind him. Who can make him run up the steps?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/97609/size7/fce4da2bddc71052a69c395326c949bc.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/97609/size7/fce4da2bddc71052a69c395326c949bc.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-58551","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-58551","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":451,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-363202","title":"Every Minute Counts","authors":["Shabnam  Minwalla"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Adil has a full hour to get ready and walk to school. But he is late every day! Where is he losing time? His friend Paro decides to help him account for every minute of the hour.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/715159/size7/650ba79042fee11ebd6f09a6ba108f43.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/715159/size7/650ba79042fee11ebd6f09a6ba108f43.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-363202","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-363202","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":452,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-16921","title":"The Doll That Bommakka Made","authors":["Praba Ram","Sheela Preuitt"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"This charming cumulative tale celebrates the tradition of hand-crafted dolls, inspired by the South Indian Thanjavur Thalai Atti Bommai. Starting with a little ball of clay, we see the fine dancing doll grow before our eyes. The rhythmic descriptive words, stacked in a delightfully repetitive way, invite children to chant along. The vibrant illustrations complete the vivid imagery.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/114328/size7/087d139e9e25a4db2e8af7c0435a63bc.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/114328/size7/087d139e9e25a4db2e8af7c0435a63bc.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-16921","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-16921","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":453,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-28266","title":"How Heavy Is Heavy?","authors":["Sukanya  Sinha"],"language":"kg","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"A stone is heavier than a feather and lighter than a rock. So is the stone heavy, or is it light? Can we know for sure how heavy (or light) a stone is? Find answers to these and other fascinating questions in this fun book about weight.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/714192/size7/f84b89b4e29caf6ef8a5b8b5e542bf4c.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/714192/size7/f84b89b4e29caf6ef8a5b8b5e542bf4c.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-28266","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-28266","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":454,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-42671","title":"The Peacock Who Wished to Fly","authors":["Alisha Berger"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Peacock is sad. He wants to be able to fly like the other birds. What happens when he starts collecting feathers?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/101406/size7/5e3b36f8678e3c72b8d78e4479ff12e6.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/101406/size7/5e3b36f8678e3c72b8d78e4479ff12e6.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-42671","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-42671","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":455,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-37272","title":"A Little Monkey and a Fish","authors":["Shannon David"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"A Little Monkey and a Fish is a story about a young, playful, and clever monkey who learns to make his way in the world by mimicking his mother. Along his journey, he must decide whether or not to take some risks. What do you think he will do?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/101337/size7/8efd990d6ebb9f677596371a2aa09e5b.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/101337/size7/8efd990d6ebb9f677596371a2aa09e5b.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-37272","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-37272","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":456,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-28951","title":"Amma, There is a Bat in My Sambar!","authors":["Menaka Raman"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Suppi is not at all happy to see a bat flying about in his house. In fact, he is quite scared of the bat.\nHow can Suppi and Amma get the bat back to her family?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/57856/size7/f1e874aeb6aad2c5558fea57c8273c6c.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/57856/size7/f1e874aeb6aad2c5558fea57c8273c6c.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-28951","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-28951","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":457,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-69028","title":"The Girl Who Thinks in Numbers: Data Warrior  Prukalpa Sankar","authors":["Shreyasi Singh"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Prukalpa Sankar loves numbers. They help her see patterns and solve community problems. How does she do this?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/718388/size7/20706d3f0f69d8952f5afdb3b86786f6.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/718388/size7/20706d3f0f69d8952f5afdb3b86786f6.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-69028","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-69028","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":458,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-37104","title":"The Tino, the Rhear and the Biger","authors":["Ashok Rajagopalan"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Tingu Tiger is not happy with his furry orange skin, so he exchanges it with Ranga Rhino. But when he wants his skin back, Ranga has already given it to Bubloo Bear! Will the tino, rhear and biger go back to being tiger, rhino and bear? Find out in this fun story about muddled up animals.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/726495/size7/0f748e0a30ec491c6c7ac54cd4157b8e.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/726495/size7/0f748e0a30ec491c6c7ac54cd4157b8e.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-37104","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-37104","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":459,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-326351","title":"A Tea Garden Party","authors":["Swati Sengupta"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Abha is going to the cool hills of Darjeeling. On the way she stops at a tea factory. She has so many questions! Is tea a leaf? Where does it grow? What makes it taste so good? Go on a tour of a tea garden and factory and find the answers to these questions with Abha.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/422097/size7/b064c2ac77aba307892edb71ceb40ca9.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/422097/size7/b064c2ac77aba307892edb71ceb40ca9.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-326351","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-326351","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":460,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-267809","title":"A Tree's Heart","authors":["Radha Rangarajan"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Did you know trees are storytellers? Listen carefully and you can hear them whisper many stories — of forest fires and rain, of summer and winter, of our past and future. Look carefully around a tree’s heartwood and you will discover many tales, like the one in this book.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/716359/size7/c8fe91246e9c51abbdb60013eab5f3df.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/716359/size7/c8fe91246e9c51abbdb60013eab5f3df.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-267809","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-267809","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":461,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-96518","title":"Peepre in the Postbox","authors":["Aditi De"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Peepre the ant finds herself in a postbox! Share her journey to discover how mail travels from one place to another.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/527530/size7/1b275e4076d102c3764850e6e59bebe6.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/527530/size7/1b275e4076d102c3764850e6e59bebe6.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-96518","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-96518","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":462,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-10395","title":"Apu's Giant Earthquake","authors":["Sudeshna  Shome Ghosh"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Did Apu’s singing cause the earth to tremble and shake? Or was it an earthquake? Find out more in this humorous and fascinating story about earthquakes.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/713578/size7/2e61153788e79629615dbd8dd46a58fc.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/713578/size7/2e61153788e79629615dbd8dd46a58fc.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-10395","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-10395","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"