nce. Won’t anyone dance with her?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/86908/size7/9e5f5a8635052315e4d550572471ac04.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/86908/size7/9e5f5a8635052315e4d550572471ac04.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-24737","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-24737","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":188,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-41047","title":"The Sunshower Song","authors":["Vinayak Varma"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"When the sun shines on a rainy day, all the animals of the forest know what’s about to happen: music and magic at the jackals’ wedding! The wedding guests each bring a scrap of sound. Some bring rhythm, and some bring tune, in this lyrical ode to the popular sunshower legend.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/722808/size7/edd852d0d4268ddc9644206749e04b7c.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/722808/size7/edd852d0d4268ddc9644206749e04b7c.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-41047","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-41047","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":189,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-27124","title":"Lazy Mama","authors":["Vidya Pradhan"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"When lazy Raghu Mama claims that he can go on wild adventures without leaving his chair, Amish and Soni are amazed. How does he do it? Can Amish and Soni go on these adventures too?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/714195/size7/3774467adccf3e2d6841cf43aa22d880.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.