90eefab9.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-104751","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-104751","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":449,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-132","title":"Daddy's Mo","authors":["Sai Keskar"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"What does Anu like the most about her dad? His Mo! Do you know what a Mo is? Actually, Anu likes everyone with a Mo. So much so that when she sees a Mo, she gets funny ideas!","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/721686/size7/0eaa2e9b2d4d4c465ba2c5e05a6f092c.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/721686/size7/0eaa2e9b2d4d4c465ba2c5e05a6f092c.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-132","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-132","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":450,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-58551","title":"Hungry on the Steps","authors":["Nandini Nayar"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Pranav is hungry. As he climbs up the steps to his house slowly, many others join the line behind him. Who can make him run up the steps?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/97609/size7/fce4da2bddc71052a69c395326c949bc.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/97609/size7/fce4da2bddc71052a69c395326c949bc.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-58551","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-58551","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":451,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-363202","title":"Every Minute Counts","authors":["Shabnam  Minwalla"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Adil has a full hour to get ready and walk to school. But he is late every day! Where is he losing time? His friend Paro decides to help him account for every minute of the hour.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/715159/size7/650ba79042fee11ebd6f09a6ba108f43.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/715159/size7/650ba79042fee11ebd6f09a6ba108f43.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-363202","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-363202","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":452,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-28266","title":"How Heavy Is Heavy?","authors":["Sukanya  Sinha"],"language":"kg","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"A stone is heavier than a feather and lighter than a rock. So is the stone heavy, or is it light? Can we know for sure how heavy (or light) a stone is? Find answers to these and other fascinating questions in this fun book about weight.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/714192/size7/f84b89b4e29caf6ef8a5b8b5e542bf4c.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/714192/size7/f84b89b4e29caf6ef8a5b8b5e542bf4c.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-28266","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-28266","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":453,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-16921","title":"The Doll That Bommakka Made","authors":["Praba Ram","Sheela Preuitt"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"This charming cumulative tale celebrates the tradition of hand-crafted dolls, inspired by the South Indian Thanjavur Thalai Atti Bommai. Starting with a little ball of clay, we see the fine dancing doll grow before our eyes. The rhythmic descriptive words, stacked in a delightfully repetitive way, invite children to chant along. The vibrant illustrations complete the vivid imagery.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/114328/size7/087d139e9e25a4db2e8af7c0435a63bc.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/114328/size7/087d139e9e25a4db2e8af7c0435a63bc.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-16921","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-16921","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":454,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-42671","title":"The Peacock Who Wished to Fly","authors":["Alisha Berger"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Peacock is sad. He wants to be able to fly like the other birds. What happens when he starts collecting feathers?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/101406/size7/5e3b36f8678e3c72b8d78e4479ff12e6.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/101406/size7/5e3b36f8678e3c72b8d78e4479ff12e6.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-42671","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-42671","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":455,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-37272","title":"A Little Monkey and a Fish","authors":["Shannon David"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"A Little Monkey and a Fish is a story about a young, playful, and clever monkey who learns to make his way in the world by mimicking his mother. Along his journey, he must decide whether or not to take some risks. What do you think he will do?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/101337/size7/8efd990d6ebb9f677596371a2aa09e5b.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/101337/size7/8efd990d6ebb9f677596371a2aa09e5b.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-37272","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-37272","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":456,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-28951","title":"Amma, There is a Bat in My Sambar!","authors":["Menaka Raman"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Suppi is not at all happy to see a bat flying about in his house. In fact, he is quite scared of the bat.\nHow can Suppi and Amma get the bat back to her family?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/57856/size7/f1e874aeb6aad2c5558fea57c8273c6c.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/57856/size7/f1e874aeb6aad2c5558fea57c8273c6c.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-28951","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-28951","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":457,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-69028","title":"The Girl Who Thinks in Numbers: Data Warrior  Prukalpa Sankar","authors":["Shreyasi Singh"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Prukalpa Sankar loves numbers. They help her see patterns and solve community problems. How does she do this?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/718388/size7/20706d3f0f69d8952f5afdb3b86786f6.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/718388/size7/20706d3f0f69d8952f5afdb3b86786f6.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-69028","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-69028","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":458,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-37104","title":"The Tino, the Rhear and the Biger","authors":["Ashok Rajagopalan"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Tingu Tiger is not happy with his furry orange skin, so he exchanges it with Ranga Rhino. But when he wants his skin back, Ranga has already given it to Bubloo Bear! Will the tino, rhear and biger go back to being tiger, rhino and bear? Find out in this fun story about muddled up animals.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/726495/size7/0f748e0a30ec491c6c7ac54cd4157b8e.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/726495/size7/0f748e0a30ec491c6c7ac54cd4157b8e.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-37104","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-37104","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":459,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-326351","title":"A Tea Garden Party","authors":["Swati Sengupta"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Abha is going to the cool hills of Darjeeling. On the way she stops at a tea factory. She has so many questions! Is tea a leaf? Where does it grow? What makes it taste so good? Go on a tour of a tea garden and factory and find the answers to these questions with Abha.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/422097/size7/b064c2ac77aba307892edb71ceb40ca9.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/422097/size7/b064c2ac77aba307892edb71ceb40ca9.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-326351","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-326351","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":460,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-267809","title":"A Tree's Heart","authors":["Radha Rangarajan"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Did you know trees are storytellers? Listen carefully and you can hear them whisper many stories — of forest fires and rain, of summer and winter, of our past and future. Look carefully around a tree’s heartwood and you will discover many tales, like the one in this book.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/716359/size7/c8fe91246e9c51abbdb60013eab5f3df.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/716359/size7/c8fe91246e9c51abbdb60013eab5f3df.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-267809","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-267809","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":461,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-96518","title":"Peepre in the Postbox","authors":["Aditi De"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Peepre the ant finds herself in a postbox! Share her journey to discover how mail travels from one place to another.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/527530/size7/1b275e4076d102c3764850e6e59bebe6.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/527530/size7/1b275e4076d102c3764850e6e59bebe6.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-96518","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-96518","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":462,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-124411","title":"Manasa Collects a Rainbow","authors":["Shalini  Srinivasan"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Manasa is on the hunt for a different kind of rainbow. Can she do it? Let’s find out. Join Manasa on her adventure.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/495523/size7/5b4c1b6586eede14f66e66af9be535ef.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/495523/size7/5b4c1b6586eede14f66e66af9be535ef.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-124411","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-124411","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":463,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-10395","title":"Apu's Giant Earthquake","authors":["Sudeshna  Shome Ghosh"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Did Apu’s singing cause the earth to tremble and shake? Or was it an earthquake? Find out more in this humorous and fascinating story about earthquakes.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/713578/size7/2e61153788e79629615dbd8dd46a58fc.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/713578/size7/2e61153788e79629615dbd8dd46a58fc.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-10395","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-10395","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":464,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-36490","title":"I Love My Mom","authors":["Stephanie  Wei"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"The girl in this story learns from her mother every day. Now she knows many things. Which of these can YOU do?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/93898/size7/5514f498477b51945a0f2ac63b7fae8b.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://stati