c.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":566,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-265508","title":"You Won't Believe Me","authors":["Jairaj Singh"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Here is a boy who likes his school a lot, but is sure that his school does not like him back. His classmates bully him. His teachers shout at him. But there is a pond full of fish — where he discovers that he’s not alone.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/524464/size7/495e026e7af09c81f3d5813cf16cdcb8.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/524464/size7/495e026e7af09c81f3d5813cf16cdcb8.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-265508","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-265508","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":567,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-162282","title":"P.S. What's up with the climate?","authors":["Bijal Vachharajani"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"It’s too hot. It’s too cold. There’s no rain. There’s too much rain. There’s less snow. There’s too much carbon in the atmosphere. Grizzly bears don’t know whether to sleep, penguins don’t know what to eat. Kangaroos are escaping forest fires, bees are groggy from all the pesticide. In a world overrun by the climate crisis, is it time to panic yet?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/234334/size7/e8a8b21f43aaa4d1a27745b56b34a5d1.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/234334/size7/e8a8b21f43aaa4d1a27745b56b34a5d1.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-162282","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-162282","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":568,"opdsId":"u