"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Gadbad Das is the son of the famous singer, Gardhab Das. He lives in a small town in India. Like his father, Gadbad is a very bad singer. Everybody knows this, except him! He does various odd jobs to survive and solves his problems musically mostly. Like this one, where there is no water for his puncture shop. Off goes Gadbad Das to find some water, but it’s not as easy as you’d think.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727059/size7/2e28482892278aceea1647757d2c7ade.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727059/size7/2e28482892278aceea1647757d2c7ade.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-63968","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-63968","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":671,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-1062","title":"Noisy Crows","authors":["Kanchan Bannerjee"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Caw! Caw! The crow in this book is calling out to young readers to read this book. This book is one of the four books in the 'Animals Around Us' series.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/704907/size7/13f658c3851393d29582f887eedc6f06.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/704907/size7/13f658c3851393d29582f887eedc6f06.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-1062","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-1062","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":672,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-612553","title":"Muthu and Kappu","authors":["Sheena Deviah"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Muthanna of Kottageri does not like black cats. They bring bad luck, he is sure. What happens when Gangu and Raja bring home the blackest of kittens?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/705618/size7/25a31473686ab2e52b88b4013188a895.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/705618/size7/25a31473686ab2e52b88b4013188a895.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-612553","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-612553","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":673,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-41199","title":"Saru and her Little Secret","authors":["Sunita Lad Bhamray"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Mai does not approve of indiscipline and Saru finds it hard to always walk the straight and narrow path. Saru often gets into trouble with Mai. What has she done this time? What will happen when Mai finds out? Read on to find out more.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/96028/size7/84cc07db945e7775faa10c9e809beeca.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/96028/size7/84cc07db945e7775faa10c9e809beeca.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-41199","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-41199","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":674,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-264337","title":"Dadi, Dadi, What Colour Do You See?","authors":["Ekta Bharti"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"When Guddu, Golu and Dadi go to the mela and try on magic glasses, they discover a whole new world of colours.\nA simple book on how primary colours interact\nto form secondary colours.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/725228/size7/7e1e5be439c3