 Why is it special? Read more to find out.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/283816/size7/c354d490842834570030304a57cdc70b.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/283816/size7/c354d490842834570030304a57cdc70b.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-216684","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-216684","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":860,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-152917","title":"Face","authors":["Little Zebra Books"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Learn the parts of the face, with the help of a whimsically illustrated group of friends.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/207389/size7/404833cf0ca7ec8115190b767c6214e8.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/207389/size7/404833cf0ca7ec8115190b767c6214e8.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-152917","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-152917","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":861,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-299399","title":"B. R. Ambedkar: A life in books","authors":["Yogesh Maitreya"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"This is the story of B. R. Ambedkar, also known as the Father of India’s Constitution. Babasaheb, as he was fondly called, was not only a visionary, an economist and a revolutionary, he was also a lifelong reader. This is the story of his love for learning and how it fuelled his journey.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727370/size7/dcf9772fbc6e7843e82e01cd5af44027.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727370/size7/dcf9772fbc6e7843e82e01cd5af44027.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-299399","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-299399","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":862,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-63546","title":"A Shade of GREEN","authors":["Rya Jetha"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"The air in the city is grey and polluted. Nayantara and Aliza feel suffocated. They dream of leaves that work day and night to produce oxygen and clean energy. Can they invent a leaf that does all that?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/718464/size7/347a0a585fadb43ad09779f4df38781d.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/718464/size7/347a0a585fadb43ad09779f4df38781d.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-63546","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-63546","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":863,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-23596","title":"The Ocean Dream","authors":["Alisha Berger"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Coral loves exploring the river. One day, she saves a rainbow fish from the river grass, and together they begin an underwater adventure.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/120475/size7/bc746f104dad3b53057ebbdadd6e1aea.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/120475/size7/bc746f104dad3b53057ebbdadd6e1aea.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-23596","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-23596","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":864,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-232639","title":"Birds That Sing Their Name","authors":["Panchapakesan Jeganathan"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"How do birds get their names? Sometimes people name them after their colours, size and food they eat. Sometimes, they get their names from the way they call or sing. Come meet some of the birds that sing their names.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/336995/size7/225fb007671ccfda5cfac7d7c762fffc.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/336995/size7/225fb007671ccfda5cfac7d7c762fffc.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-232639","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-232639","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":865,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-90","title":"Goloo the Circle","authors":["Jagdish Joshi"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Goloo opens your eyes to the circular world around you! Children can play a game too - how many circles can you see? You need no pens, paper or dice - all you have to do is take turns and keep score.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/721846/size7/96939c817bb3119d56ea3a22243ea8b9.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/721846/size7/96939c817bb3119d56ea3a22243ea8b9.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-90","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-90","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":866,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-104345","title":"The Nose of all Noses","authors":["Meera Ganapathi"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Zahra’s Dadima has an unusually large nose. It picks up scents that others cannot even imagine. Zahra wants a super nose too. Find out what happens when Dadima and Zahra take a deep sniff of attar and embark on an adventure to train for a super nose.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/179725/size7/15f364d92111de41f9eee020024db06a.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/179725/size7/15f364d92111de41f9eee020024db06a.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-104345","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-104345","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":867,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-85556","title":"Poon Poon...","authors":["Swagata Sen Pillai"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Smelly or loud - farts find a way to make themselves known. Whether they come as a surprise or as a relief, they do feel good! A terrific poem about farts, a secret that everyone knows.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727097/size7/8a2cbd3cbde95b072abeee5d2417325d.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727097/size7/8a2cbd3cbde95b072abeee5d2417325d.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-85556","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-85556","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":868,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-162968","title":"Father, Son and Donkey","authors":["Tagel Aboneh"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"A folktale of father, son and donkey!","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/231194/size7/4d0f485ed35e5661aa44f64fe7e03a65.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/231194/size7/4d0f485ed35e5661aa44f64fe7e03a65.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-162968","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-162968","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":869,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-292656","title":"Earth, Our Home","authors":["Anushka  Ravishankar","Karthika Nair","Salil  Chaturvedi","Sampurna Chattarji"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"The story of Earth is the story of life. It is also a story of loss, one worsened by climate change. But while the climate crisis can be a story of devastation, the work being done to mitigate it, to adapt to it, brings hope. And reminds us, our future is in our hands. The verses in this book tell these stories, in the voices of the orangutan, the Hasdeo Arand forest, the Gangetic dolphin and the Pondicherry shark.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/721331/size7/772b3d930ec8af783d7a1a163c6b23de.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/721331/size7/772b3d930ec8af783d7a1a163c6b23de.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-292656","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-292656","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":870,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-255063","title":"This is Where We Live","authors":["Manjari Chakravarti"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"An ordinary day unfolds through the eyes of Jugnu and Noorie, two felines in Shantiniketan—early morning rays slant in through the windows, fish and fruit sellers do their rounds, and children leave for school. However, as the hours slip by, and kal baisakhi, the spring storm, sweeps in all of a sudden, can the day be anything but extraordinary? Stop and stare at Jugnu and Noorie’s everyday world, discover the tiny details and peel each layer in this wordless and slow picture book.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/346798/size7/66152c7f4dd3c710a56f60d5e17054c2.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/346798/size7/66152c7f4dd3c710a56f60d5e17054c2.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-255063","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-255063","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":871,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-130628","title":"When I Grow Up, I'll Have a House","authors":["Jerry Pinto"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"A verse book about all the wondrous things that make a house a home.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727186/size7/4ae70d26ced5fa58a2b4c132364c25c8.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727186/size7/4ae70d26ced5fa58a2b4c132364c25c8.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-130628","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-130628","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":872,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-590649","title":"My Yellow Umbrella","authors":["Poojana Prasanna"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"An umbrella can brighten up a grey and rainy day. But it can also be so many things. Take a walk to find out.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/706685/size7/d283c7549928879966054e39f420f4ad.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/706685/size7/d283c7549928879966054e39f420f4ad.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-590649","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-590649","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":873,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-191429","title":"The Guest","authors":["Sanghamitra Ghosh"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Tarapodo met zamindar Motilal babu. He was going to his village with his family. Tarapodo with his cooking and serving skill came very close to Motilal babu’s family.  Will Tarapodo stay with the family forever because they love him?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/331521/size7/5e8f592d39309c63a839add198dbba4a.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/331521/size7/5e8f592d39309c63a839add198dbba4a.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-191429","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-191429","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":874,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-106392","title":"Megan and the Mystery of the Moving Rock","authors":["C G Salamander"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Megan is very busy. She has to solve the mystery of Frits the missing cat. Even if it means chasing a scary rock creature into a strange new world.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/157760/size7/6cdf56d742712f6c42562ce908f7bd12.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/157760/size7/6cdf56d742712f6c42562ce908f7bd12.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-106392","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-106392","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":875,"opdsId