aunt and her nephew.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/117615/size7/2b5f77b28bb196dfb73d2b136890b5b0.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/117615/size7/2b5f77b28bb196dfb73d2b136890b5b0.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-44201","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-44201","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":276,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-11283","title":"Kalpana's Cycle","authors":["Sowmya Rajendran"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Kalpana is learning to cycle, but it isn’t easy at all! She falls over and over again, even hurting herself. Does she finally learn to cycle? Does she give up? A heartwarming story about the importance of trying.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/713553/size7/3ad6ce1af3d4d426a2cb31704c688037.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/713553/size7/3ad6ce1af3d4d426a2cb31704c688037.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-11283","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-11283","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":277,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-122433","title":"Dog's Day","authors":["Sunando C"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"What does a dog do all day? This wordless book gives us a glimpse into the life of a human's best friend.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727177/size7/3759994b1ddc2714678973dcf02b3769.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727177/size7/3759994b1ddc2714678973dcf02b3769.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-122433","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-122433","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":278,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-103017","title":"Hide and Seek","authors":["All Children Reading Cambodia"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Dodo plays Hide-and-seek with mum, what can Dodo find?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/150992/size7/efc8b1d281e3853492ad0e1ee0651268.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/150992/size7/efc8b1d281e3853492ad0e1ee0651268.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-103017","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-103017","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":279,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-14051","title":"The Best Thing Ever","authors":["Melissa  Fagan","Stefania Origgi"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Muzi loves to build with his toys. But when he leaves them behind to travel to uGogo’s house, he discovers something very special about the world. And he learns something new about himself.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/118153/size7/bc2ba70b6ef08fef7c20b01264e48156.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/118153/size7/bc2ba70b6ef08fef7c20b01264e48156.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-14051","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-14051","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":280,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-93901","title":"Making Friends with Snakes (But from a Distance)","authors":["Rohan Chakravarty"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Naagin and Dhaman are here to make friends with you, but from a distance. After all, they are snakes. Find out everything you wanted to know about these beautiful reptiles and also learn how to stay safe and let snakes slither to safety!","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727062/size7/1434dec5e0d6a834070c3f6555c82bc2.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727062/size7/1434dec5e0d6a834070c3f6555c82bc2.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-93901","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-93901","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":281,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-31137","title":"Who Made the Tomato Chutney?","authors":["Kavitha Mandana"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Tara and Ravi go to the market to buy fruits and vegetables. But each time one fruit gets squashed! The concept of sorting is introduced through heavy and light objects. \nThe illustrations in the book were made using bits of paper, old magazines and paper bags that were collected - not squished - under mattresses.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/717010/size7/0bef1395055c740659b27b823aeea0ac.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/717010/size7/0bef1395055c740659b27b823aeea0ac.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-31137","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-31137","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":282,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-10058","title":"Biju Spins Some Magic","authors":["Jaya Jaitly"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Biju and his family are weavers in rural Odisha. They create beautiful fabrics to sell in the cities of India and abroad. This is the tale of Biju’s adventures when he accompanies his father to Delhi to sell the saris, and in the process impresses a city boy with his skill. Jaya Jaitly’s fun-filled story is illustrated by Bhramara Nayak in the patachitra style.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/524535/size7/2d6162e002a3bf3ad6834ac1a6050a54.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/524535/size7/2d6162e002a3bf3ad6834ac1a6050a54.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-10058","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-10058","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":283,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-212","title":"The Tree","authors":["Madhav Chavan"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"The tale of how a tree grows from a tiny seed.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/722234/size7/94ca99b3484af2b07528283397858dba.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/722234/size7/94ca99b3484af2b07528283397858dba.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-212","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-212","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":284,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-110883","title":"Water Dance","authors":["Sean D'mello"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Guddu can dance to anything. Today he has found music in water and can’t stop doing a jig as he makes his way down a stream. A story that introduces water bodies and celebrates the joy of water.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/721324/size7/5a1f19ca4a60e1aaf734bc03f0c3be11.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/721324/size7/5a1f19ca4a60e1aaf734bc03f0c3be11.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-110883","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-110883","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":285,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-754","title":"Marching to Freedom","authors":["Subhadra Sen Gupta"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Mahatma Gandhi and his followers have decided to march to Dandi to protest against the unfair salt tax imposed by the British. 9-year-old Dhani who lives at the Sabarmati Ashram wants to go too. This tale captures the spirit behind the momentous event that inspired millions of Indians to join the struggle for Independence.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/703496/size7/e199c7b11d12f05af68f797c629d0af3.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/703496/size7/e199c7b11d12f05af68f797c629d0af3.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-754","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-754","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":286,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-339149","title":"Have You Ever Climbed a Tree?","authors":["Priyadarshini Gogoi"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Have you ever climbed a tree? Riniki dreams of climbing trees all over the country. Join her as she scrambles, crawls and clambers on the jackfruit, the chinar, the khejri and other trees.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/495551/size7/2d67536698e82439794800d91ba40bef.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/495551/size7/2d67536698e82439794800d91ba40bef.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-339149","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-339149","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":287,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-342334","title":"Plants Are Everywhere","authors":["Ritu Desai"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Plants grow everywhere — on high mountains, on arid lands, and even under the sea. Explore different types of plants in this book.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/434073/size7/3927b068f2f1009ae79ef445c56eb5be.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/434073/size7/3927b068f2f1009ae79ef445c56eb5be.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-342334","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-342334","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":288,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-4314","title":"How Do Aeroplanes Fly?","authors":["Aditi Sarawagi"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Sarla wished she could fly high like an eagle or like an aeroplane. Of course you can fly, said her new teacher. Here, Sarla shares all that she has learnt about flight and aeroplanes.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/711239/size7/76fe943740d2496ae267805d81599763.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/711239/size7/76fe943740d2496ae267805d81599763.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-4314","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-4314","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}