orest. They know each zigzag path, each large sal and mohua tree, each pug mark of the mongoose and the tiger, and so much more! Young Burli is beginning to read the signs of nature, but is she ready to face the most dangerous ordeal of her life?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/99425/size7/17c509cd79601054fa8341f61478f16a.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/99425/size7/17c509cd79601054fa8341f61478f16a.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-41052","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-41052","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1076,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-613804","title":"The Porcupine and Elephant","authors":["Lanu Tsudir"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"On a warm day, an elephant and a porcupine are locked in a silly showdown, each claiming to be the strongest and the mightiest. As they quarrel, an unsuspecting third party can’t help but chuckle at their antics. How will this squabble end?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/678630/size7/73e5495aa31ae4110d5ad5b3b3afb153.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/678630/size7/73e5495aa31ae4110d5ad5b3b3afb153.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-613804","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-613804","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1077,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-141","title":"Going to a Wedding","authors":["Rukmini Banerji"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Children always like to share their experience with others. Going to a wedding shows how enjoyable the experiences can be.","coverUrl":"https://s