":"Is Piku’s Pishi made up of magic? After all, Pishi can turn into different people. Piku discovers the world of theatre and finds himself making a few friends too!","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/712882/size7/7910af3bbb76b165a9e341132e1e9af2.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/712882/size7/7910af3bbb76b165a9e341132e1e9af2.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-641668","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-641668","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1613,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-613224","title":"Apjon Apjon","authors":["Iwakani Challam"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"When fluffy clouds make different shapes in the sky, children gather to sing a merry song. What do you sing when you see shapes in the clouds? \nApjon! Apjon!","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/678033/size7/9bf9c0f0b9cbfba3c3a2ffe8c403072f.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/678033/size7/9bf9c0f0b9cbfba3c3a2ffe8c403072f.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-613224","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-613224","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1614,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-643377","title":"Bumbb: The Magical Cylinder","authors":["Meenu Thomas"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Amita and Ninad are curious. Their neighbour Vilas doesn’t visit the forest to collect firewood as often as he used to. And his wife Varsha doesn’t spend all her time in front of the chulha to heat water. Their children say that a magical\ncylinder gives the neighbours hot water in no time. Could it be true?","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727685/size7/65b7fb7fd712915b6dca84af7129a461.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/727685/size7/65b7fb7fd712915b6dca84af7129a461.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-643377","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-643377","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1615,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-49725","title":"Byantaka and the Dead Pot","authors":["Cornelius Wambi  Gulere"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Byantaka, the heardsman desperately wanted a big pot, so he decided to trick his neighbour to get it.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/126985/size7/5965d9e0665db032c3965c2545bff208.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/126985/size7/5965d9e0665db032c3965c2545bff208.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-49725","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-49725","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1616,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-674203","title":"Ira's Monsoon Feast","authors":["Mukta Patil"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"It’s time for a feast! Pull on your raincoats, grab your umbrellas and join Ira and her family as they go on a foraging and harvesting walk.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/756617/size7/e375e25b085824c06bfe636045bb7871.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/756617/size7/e375e25b085824c06bfe636045bb7871.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-674203","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-674203","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1617,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-650968","title":"Khampai Becomes a Yaopa","authors":["Longang  Luklem"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"In life, one experiences love, joy, and loss. Join Khampai on an emotional journey, where he explores his grandfather’s craft, embraces his legacy, and finds himself on a path of self-discovery.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/754813/size7/545facfa367d73e231d129ac0486b720.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/754813/size7/545facfa367d73e231d129ac0486b720.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-650968","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-650968","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1618,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-652921","title":"Lost in Ultapani","authors":["Chalini Basumatary"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"In a state of being lost, an unexpected friendship leads the way through the darkness. Explore the rich flora and fauna of Ultapani forest as baby elephant finds his way back to his family.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/756375/size7/5665d0763c959a76d276838e338f1101.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/756375/size7/5665d0763c959a76d276838e338f1101.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-652921","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-652921","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1619,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-666607","title":"Keep It Up, Number 6!","authors":["Pankaj Saikia"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Bulbuli and Maina are a little scared of Number 6. What with the rooster’s magnificent ability to chase  every single being on the farm, his awe-inspiring looks and loud clucks. But the siblings discover that even  the most fearsome of creatures can surprise us!","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/751419/size7/31a945867e2d99c4d829ecc38b6bccf9.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/751419/size7/31a945867e2d99c4d829ecc38b6bccf9.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-666607","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-666607","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1620,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-653037","title":"Nungpak Thabi vs Tumurak","authors":["Linthoi Chanu"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"A fierce battle seems imminent as Tumurak, the towering hill by the edge of Pumlen Lake, mocks Nungpak Thabi, the smaller hill. Who do you think will win? Read more to find out.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/750807/size7/1c8d9adc2a2790c2bacfa97d1985867b.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/750807/size7/1c8d9adc2a2790c2bacfa97d1985867b.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-653037","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-653037","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1621,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-642225","title":"Where Is Goggayya?","authors":["Srinath Perur"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Amma, Ajja and Atte always call Goggayya when Putti is up to some mischief. But what does Goggayya look like? Where does Goggayya hide? Putti wants to know.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/723784/size7/e7ef7449b13aac59bce727272b35da36.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/723784/size7/e7ef7449b13aac59bce727272b35da36.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-642225","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-642225","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1622,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-651907","title":"Snow Ice Cream","authors":["Tashi Chong Sherpa"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"In the village of Uttarey, little Dolma patiently awaits the arrival of snowfall so that she can enjoy the delicious snow ice-cream. Does she get to taste the winter treat? Read this little poem to find out.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/754816/size7/0dd726611b1a71b8f3521aab4f361fe3.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/754816/size7/0dd726611b1a71b8f3521aab4f361fe3.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-651907","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-651907","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1623,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-651910","title":"Yapom","authors":["Moge Basar"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"A lonely Yapom lives high up on a tree. One day, she meets a little boy. Their time together unfolds the journey of the yapom and her\nlonging for companionship and friendship.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/754815/size7/a2969c4be473bd87e010df4ac38c0ca4.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/754815/size7/a2969c4be473bd87e010df