la Foundation"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"A warm invitation into the homes of Northeast India through a delightful collection of kitchen illustrations.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/754776/size7/4c4fac470c177e9e6b8966c4d62e5018.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/754776/size7/4c4fac470c177e9e6b8966c4d62e5018.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-657262","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-657262","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1636,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-665305","title":"The tale of Pukshi","authors":["Linthoi Chanu"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"In ancient Samutak, Haokha Nongkha Ngamba's daughter Wandengnu wished to participate in the traditional Pam Yanba ritual. Delighted by her interest, Haokha Nongkha gives his daughter a gourd of honey to share with her friends on their journey. However, he forgets to tell Wangdengnu a small detail... that the gourd was magical.","coverUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/754788/size7/399015e0004db0c53f8552a716ccc32f.jpg","thumbnailUrl":"https://static.storyweaver.org.in/illustration_crops/754788/size7/399015e0004db0c53f8552a716ccc32f.jpg","acquisitions":[{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/pdf/SW-665305","type":"application/pdf+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"},{"href":"https://storyweaver.org.in/api/v0/story/epub/SW-665305","type":"application/epub+zip","rel":"http://opds-spec.org/acquisition"}]},{"id":1637,"opdsId":"urn:uuid:SW-665304","title":"Lungdai and the Hornbill","authors":["Thomas Malsom"],"language":"","readingLevel":"","publisher":"","summary":"Lungdai is frustrated! The hornbill bird keeps taking away all the fruits from his Pipi’s garden. They belong to hi